The Football Federation of Cambodia, chaired by Sao Sokha, has postponed all four of its ongoing football events, including two national championships, a women's league and a women's league. The Tiger Futsal Cup includes the 2020 Under-15 and Under-18 Championship.
The Shooting Federation of Cambodia issued a notice on Wednesday postponing the 2020 Shooting Championships to December, with the event originally scheduled for the 28th. November 29, 2020 at the 911 Special Forces Command, Phnom Penh.
At the same time, the Dance and Dance Federation of Cambodia, chaired by Lok Chumteav Nhem Morakot, also announced the postponement of the 2020 National Dance Competition, which is scheduled to be held at the National Stadium from 14 to 14 days. November 15, and the federation has not yet set a new date.
Similarly, the Khmer Boxing Federation has also announced the postponement of the Khmer National Boxing Championship 2020, which is scheduled to be held from 16 to 20 November, and in addition, Mr. Tem Mean, the federation's president, told the Post that private weekend boxing matches on Bayon CNC, Channel 5, PNN, Town and Ek Phnom arenas in Battambang had also been suspended.
The first national primary school sports competition in 2020, which is scheduled to be held again from November 20 to 29, 2020, after being postponed for the first time for several months, has been postponed by the Department of Student Sports. The second time, without setting a new date yet.
The suspension and postponement of the above competition is to participate in the prevention and control of the recurrence of Kovid 19 in Cambodia in accordance with the letter No. 223 of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for the Fight against Kovid 19 and letter 63. Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, dated November 8, 2020, stipulating the suspension of all sports or exercise gatherings and the temporary entry and exit of the National Olympic Stadium. Emergency.
